--- a/crates/hivezilla/README.md
+++ b/crates/hivezilla/README.md
@@ -122,15 +122,25 @@
 The NAS pipeline can run independent legacy registry-reuse range heads in
 parallel with `--legacy-compact-concurrency` (default `1`). These lanes remain
 mutually exclusive with downloads, ordinary scans, and finalizers. Admission
-reserves the four reused registry sidecars plus 384 MiB per epoch, with a 1 GiB
-minimum, in addition to `--memory-reserve-mib`.
+uses explicit CPU and aggregate disk-I/O reservations; these are scheduler
+budgets, not kernel-enforced throttles. It also reserves the four reused
+registry sidecars plus 384 MiB per epoch, with a 1 GiB minimum, in addition to
+`--memory-reserve-mib`.
 
 ```bash
 cargo run -p blockzilla-hivezilla -- nas-pipeline \
-  --legacy-compact-concurrency 2 \
+  --legacy-compact-concurrency 4 \
+  --legacy-compact-cpu-cores-per-worker 1 \
+  --legacy-compact-cpu-budget-cores 8 \
+  --legacy-compact-io-mib-per-sec-per-worker 120 \
+  --legacy-compact-io-budget-mib-per-sec 250 \
   --memory-reserve-mib 1536
 ```
 
+This example admits at most two legacy lanes because the 250 MiB/s I/O budget
+is the limiting resource. Larger memory/disk candidates are skipped without
+blocking smaller independent range heads.
+
 ## Hetzner sizing
 
 Use `estimate-hetzner` before renting machines. The default model uses epoch

